      "caption": {
        "known": true,
        "value": "Rune discovered by the noble Goldmask.\nUsed to restore the fractured Elden Ring when brandished by the Elden Lord.\n\nA rune of transcendental ideology which will attempt to perfect the Golden Order.\n\nThe current imperfection of the Golden Order, or instability of ideology, can be blamed upon the fickleness of the gods no better than men. That is the fly in the ointment.",
        "provenance": {
          "source": "legacy_db_data",
          "method": "copied from legacy ItemTexts.Caption"
        }
      },
      "description": {
        "known": true,
        "value": "Can be used to mend the shattered Elden Ring",
        "provenance": {
          "source": "legacy_db_data",
          "method": "copied from legacy ItemTexts.Description"
        }
      },
      "location": {
        "known": true,
        "value": "Obtaining this item, like the other mending runes, will not affect any other ending.; The last part of the item's description while nuanced does deviate from the Japanese text by a considerable margin. A more straightforward translation of the JP text would be \" The imperfection of the current Golden Order is a result of a wavering perspective. There is no need for a god with a human heart, this was the flaw in the Order \".",
        "provenance": {
          "source": "legacy_db_data",
          "method": "copied from legacy ItemTexts.Location"
        }
      },
